1... Nf6 ( 1... e6 ) 2. Bxf7+ { Kt — K 5 would also give White the advantage, the threat being of course if B × Q; 2 B × P mate. Nor does B — R 5 help matters, because of 2 Q × B, 1... B — K 3 leaves Black with the inferior position. But White's move in the text secures an immediate material advantage, and the beginner at any rate should never miss such an opportunity for the sake of a speculative advantage in position. } ( 2. Ne5 Bxd1 ( 2... Be6 ) 3. Bxf7# ) 2... Kxf7 3. Ne5+ *

